            <link>https://sosotalayvadze-dotcom.github.io/call-copilot-updates/</link>
            <sparkle:version>13.0.17</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>13.0-test</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.2</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Version 13 — English and Turkish</h3>
<ul>
<li>Choose the spoken language: English or Turkish. A small EN/TR switch is on the main screen next to the Call / Briefing / History tabs, and the same choice is in Settings → Spoken Language. The app remembers it.</li>
<li>Switch during a call: one click (or the shortcut) changes the language for your microphone, the customer and the answers. The call, the microphone and WhatsApp keep running, and everything said before stays; the next answer uses it, in the new language.</li>
<li>Keyboard shortcut from any app (WhatsApp, Chrome, Zoom): Control-Option-L by default. Change it or turn it off in Settings.</li>
<li>Turkish answers are written in natural spoken Turkish with Turkish letters; words like website, hosting and domain, names and your prices stay exactly as they are. The app itself stays in English.</li>
<li>The status beside the switch shows what is really happening: "TR — Listening", "Switching Language", "Recognition Unavailable" or "Microphone Unavailable".</li>
<li>Settings → Language test: speak a sentence in English or Turkish and see the text, or test one answer in that language, without a call.</li>
<li>If your Mac cannot recognize Turkish for one side, the app says so instead of pretending; the test report lists every switch and how long it took.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Version 12.3</h3>
<ul>
<li>Connected sentences ("Facebook works fine for us. Don't need anything else.") get one answer, never while the customer is still talking.</li>
<li>Common moments are answered at once without the AI: Facebook, "happy as we are", "no time for extra stuff", "go ahead, 20 seconds".</li>
<li>"No time for extra stuff" means the work, not the call: never asks for 20 seconds again.</li>
<li>When the AI is busy or slow (over 1.2 s), the approved line appears instead of nothing; a busy provider is paused for a while.</li>
<li>Your misheard microphone words ("Greg") no longer confuse the copilot.</li>
<li>If the AI is too slow on an unusual question, you get an honest "Good question, I'll confirm that" line instead of a sales line.</li>
<li>The test report shows where the time went: hearing the customer vs. getting the answer, and how many answers were instant.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
